    "body": "Groundwork for pointing **fumola.org** at the Fumola Pages site. No behaviour change today.\n\n### Why\n\n`prebundle.js` hard-codes one published URL for the wasm runtime:\n\n```js\nglue: \"https://adapton.github.io/fumola/fumola_wasm.js\",\nwasm: \"https://adapton.github.io/fumola/fumola_wasm_bg.wasm\",\n```\n\nOnce `Adapton/fumola` takes `fumola.org` as its Pages custom domain, those URLs 301 to `https://fumola.org/...`. A GitHub Pages custom-domain redirect carries **no `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header** \u2014 verified against a live example (`pytorch.github.io/examples/`, whose org site is CNAME'd to docs.pytorch.org) \u2014 and a CORS-mode `import()` must pass the CORS check on *every* hop of a redirect chain, not just the final response. The runtime files themselves do serve `access-control-allow-origin: *`; it's the redirect in front of them that doesn't.\n\nSo the old URL works before the switch and fails after; the new one fails before and works after. Neither spans it, which would leave the deployed preview without its published-runtime fallback for as long as the two sides are out of step.\n\n### What\n\n`LOCAL` / `PUBLISHED` become a `SOURCES` list, tried in order \u2014 local, then `fumola.org`, then `adapton.github.io` \u2014 and the promise chain becomes a loop. Local stays first, so working on Fumola and Hazel together is unchanged. Whichever published URL is live answers; the other fails fast and costs one request.\n\nWhen every source fails, `loadError` now names all of them and what each said, instead of only the last error.\n\n### After the domain settles\n\nThe `adapton.github.io` entry will only ever redirect, and should be dropped.\n\n### Checking it\n\nOpen the preview and look at the console: it now logs `runtime loaded from <name>`, and `window.fumola.source()` returns that name. Before the domain moves, expect `adapton.github.io`; after, `fumola.org`.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
